title: Rerun of the header board under the refined Atelier process gave a structurally different, accepted result
summary: |-
  The same founder problem ("no consistent layout or design on these elements") was run twice.

  First run, with Luna improvised in the main thread and no gates: three options that were the same toolbar restyled. The founder called them "lacking".

  Second run, with Luna spawned and the audit, scope and distinctness gates, a real "Now" column and Mika vetting:
  - The audit found that the header had drifted from 4 specified elements to 12, at five control heights.
  - It found duplicates: the voice pill with Start voice, theme ×3, Mods ×3.
  - It found a stale idle note using the retired word "Ambient".
  - It produced three options on distinct axes: what the header is for (command line), how status is carried (kernel band), and where tools live (wordmark menu).
  - Mika attached concerns to each option and recorded one Luna/Mika disagreement for the founder.
  - The founder picked C (wordmark menu) without further revision.

  The gates changed the outcome, not just its polish.
symbols_touched:
  - '#atelier-design'
  - '#gui'
learnings:
  - An audit with file:line evidence surfaces drift and duplicates that a styling pass hides.
  - Requiring each option to name a structural axis produced options the founder could actually choose between.
